, Consulting 22.7%, Interest Income 0.1%, Total 100%). Deductible Expenses by Category breaks down correctly (Salaries, Rent, Insurance, Travel, Office Supplies, Marketing, Utilities, Software, Total $36,485.99). All Tax-Related Transactions table lists all 18 tax-marked transactions. Year selector (2022-2026) works and correctly filters data per year.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Filtering by Type=Income showed only income rows; adding Category=Consulting further narrowed to consulting income rows; adding date range Dec 1-31 2024 narrowed to only December consulting income transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"New transaction retained showing Aug 20, 2026, Test Consulting Invoice QA, Consulting, INV-TEST-1, +$1,500.00, ✓ tax status.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Edit form does not pre-populate the Category field for existing transactions\", \"actual\": \"Opening the Edit dialog for the 'Aug Test Income Small' transaction (which has Category='Consulting' clearly shown in the table row) showed the Category combobox displaying the placeholder 'Select category' instead of 'Consulting'. All other fields (Type, Date, Description, Amount, Tax Related) pre-populated correctly. If a user edits amount/description without noticing/reselecting category, saving would silently blank the category (compounded by the previously-confirmed CS-23 bug that blank categories are accepted without validation). This was previously missed when FT-7 was recorded PASS using a different transaction where category had just been explicitly set via that same edit form; re-testing on an independently created transaction reveals the pre-population defect.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Created a new category 'QA Test Category' (Type=Expense, Color=Blue) via Add Category dialog — appeared correctly under Expense Categories with 0 transactions/$0 total. Edited it via Edit Category dialog (pre-populated Name='QA Test Category', Type='Expense' correctly), renamed to 'QA Test Category Renamed' and changed color to Teal — update reflected immediately in the list. Deleted it via Delete button, confirmed via alertdialog ('Are you sure you want to delete this category? Transactions using this category will not be deleted.'), clicked Delete — category removed from the list (verified via DOM text search returning false).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Add form for Income type listed only income categories (Sales Revenue, Consulting, Interest Income, Other Income); Edit form for Expense type listed only expense categories (Office Supplies, Rent, Utilities, Salaries, Marketing, Travel, Software, Insurance). Assigned category (Consulting, then Office Supplies) was retained with the transaction after save/edit.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Toggled Tax Related switch on during creation and during edit (off->on); resulting row Tax column showed ✓ after each save, reflecting the toggled status.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Combined Type=Income + Category=Consulting + Date range (Dec 2024) + search \\\"Strategy\\\" narrowed to exactly 1 transaction satisfying all criteria. Clicking Clear Filters restored the full 18-row set with original totals (+$47,592.50 / -$36,485.99).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Submitting Add Transaction form with empty Description and Amount did not create a transaction; both fields carry native required validation (validationMessage \\\"Please fill out this field.\\\") blocking submission and identifying missing fields.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid date range not rejected with explanation\", \"actual\": \"Setting From=2024-12-31 and To=2024-12-01 (start date later than end date) was accepted without any validation error. The page silently displayed a generic 'No transactions found / Try adjusting your filters' empty-state message identical to what appears for any valid-but-empty filter combination, with no indication that the date range itself is invalid. Checked full page text via DOM query for words like 'invalid', 'start date', 'end date', 'later than' — none found.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing category not blocked or identified\", \"actual\": \"Submitted a new Expense transaction (\\\"Test No Category\\\", $100) with no category selected. The transaction was created successfully and appears in the table with a blank Category cell instead of being rejected or flagged to the user.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-24\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Deleting a category with existing assigned transactions is not blocked or reassigned\", \"actual\": \"Attempted to delete the 'Utilities' category which had 1 assigned transaction ('Electric Bill', -$285.00). The confirmation dialog only warned 'Transactions using this category will not be deleted' (i.e., transactions are kept) but did not block deletion or offer reassignment. Confirming the delete succeeded immediately — the category was removed from the Categories page. Checking the Transactions page afterward showed the 'Electric Bill' row now has a blank/empty Category cell (previously 'Utilities'), confirming the transaction was left with an orphaned/undefined category reference instead of the deletion being blocked or requiring reassignment to another category.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added a current-month (Aug 25, 2026) Income transaction ($300, Consulting). Dashboard immediately reflected: Monthly Income $0→$300, Net Profit/Loss $0→$300, and Recent Transactions list now shows 'Aug Test Income Small' at the top with correct amount/date/category.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited the Aug 25, 2026 transaction to toggle Tax Related switch OFF. Transactions table immediately showed blank Tax column (no checkmark). Navigating to Tax Summary (year 2026) confirmed: Total Taxable Income $0.00, Net Taxable Income $0.00, 'No taxable income recorded for 2026', 'All Tax-Related Transactions: 0 transactions / No tax-related transactions for 2026' — correctly excluding the now non-tax-related transaction. (Previously with tax=true, the same transaction showed as $300.00 taxable income, 1 transaction.)\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding the $300 'Aug Test Income Small' transaction under the Consulting category, the Categories page shows Consulting category with '4 transactions' and Total '$11,100' — correctly incremented from the original 3 transactions / $10,800 baseline (confirmed from Tax Summary 2024 data: Consulting total was $10,800). Category transaction count and total dynamically reflect new transactions.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicked 'Print Report' button on Tax Summary page (2024 data loaded). No JavaScript errors were thrown (console: 0 errors, 5 warnings, unchanged before/after). Page remained fully rendered and functional after the action (verified via full snapshot showing all tax summary content intact).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Transactions table shows Date, Description, Category, Reference, Amount, and Tax columns for each row, and a Total Income / Total Expenses summary below the table for the current result set.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-21\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After adding a $300 Aug 25, 2026 Income (Consulting) transaction: Dashboard Monthly Income=$300, Monthly Expenses=$0, Net Profit/Loss=$300, Recent Transactions shows it correctly at top. Reports page (August 2026) shows Total Income=$300, Total Expenses=$0, Net Profit/Loss=+$300, Income by Category shows Consulting=$300, Expenses by Category shows 'No expenses this period' — all figures accurately match the single underlying transaction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Chart axis labels lack precision to distinguish non-zero values from zero\", \"actual\": \"After adding a $300 Aug 2026 income transaction, the 'Income vs Expenses' bar chart rendered a bar spanning nearly the full chart height (SVG path y from 9 to 221, i.e. near-maximum), confirming a real non-zero value is plotted. However, all 5 Y-axis gridline labels read '$0k' (verified via DOM query of .recharts-yAxis tick text nodes: [\\\\\\\"$0k\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"$0k\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"$0k\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"$0k\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"$0k\\\\\\\"]). The axis label formatter appears to divide by 1000 and round/floor without decimal precision, so any value under $500 (and in this case even $300 as the chart's max) is displayed identically to zero, making the chart unreadable/misleading for small-value periods.\", \"evidence\": null}]}"
      }
